Development Stack & Best Practices
	•	TanStack Query (React Query) with Axios for every API call.
	•	Use Axios interceptors for token handling, global error catching.
	•	Proper React Context or Redux Toolkit setup if global state is required.
	•	Follow environment-based logging:
	•	console.log for dev only using process.env.NODE_ENV.
	•	Remove all logs in production.

⸻

✅ Form Management & Validation
	•	Use React Hook Form for all forms.
	•	Add Yup / Zod schema-based validation for forms.
	•	Display proper inline error messages for each field.
	•	Disable submit button during loading.
	•	Prevent multiple submissions.

⸻

✅ Code Cleanliness
	•	Remove all unused code, imports, and console logs.
	•	Ensure component structure is modular and reusable.
	•	Folder structure follows feature-based separation.

⸻

✅ UI/UX Consistency
	•	All loading states have Skeleton Loaders.
	•	All async calls wrapped in Error Boundary or try-catch.
	•	Use Toast / Snackbar for user feedback (success, error, warning).
	•	Display empty state with fallback messages when no data is available.

⸻

✅ Table Functionalities
	•	All tables must support:
	•	Pagination
	•	Sorting
	•	Filtering
	•	Search (debounced if needed)
	•	Row-level actions (edit, active/inactive, view)
	•	Export

⸻

✅ Security Checks
	•	All API calls must have JWT / Token Authorization.
	•	Protect all routes with Auth Guards (PrivateRoute or middleware).
	•	Role-based access checks for modules/submenus.
	•	Sanitize all user inputs before submission.
	•	Escape HTML where needed to avoid XSS.

⸻

✅ Export  Functionality
	•	Ensure Export to CSV/Excel works with applied filters.
	•	Import supports file type validation, duplicate detection, and error summary.
	•	Show proper success/failure report on import.

⸻

✅ Notifications / Alerts
	•	Notification alerts shown via in-app toast + notification dropdown.
	•	Unread count shown in header.
 	•	Notification persists even if user reloads.

⸻

✅ Accessibility & Responsiveness
 	•	Proper focus handling and aria-labels for screen readers.
	•	Responsive layout for all screen sizes.

⸻

✅ Testing & Edge Cases
	•	Handle edge cases: no data, invalid inputs, slow network.
	•	Test all modules with both valid and invalid API data.
	•	Check all conditional UI states (loading, error, empty, success).
	•	Mobile responsiveness tested.


